<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yeongnyu of Goguryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/642">642</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yeongnyu of Goguryeo was the twenty-seventh king of Goguryeo, reigning from 618 to 642. He sought peace with the newly founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> and exchanged prisoners from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> wars, while ordering a long defensive wall along the frontier. In 642 the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yeon-gaesomun">Yeon Gaesomun</a> killed him and more than a hundred officials and placed King Bojang on the throne.</p></div>
